#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdadd355-0ce5-598a-b9cd-f189ccfb7ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents"}] :question/id #uuid "6ce1d2ce-e99a-5f5c-a698-3f744805ef24" :question/math-academy-id "e-12921" :question/problem "Calculate $(-3)^3 \\div 6$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we compute the exponents:\n\n$$\n(-3)^{3}_(⏟)_(-27) \\div 6 = (-27) \\div 6\n$$\n\nThen, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-27) \\div 6 &=  \\\\\n((-27))/(6) &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{27}{6} &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{27 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} &=  \\\\\n&= - \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0c74c4-8496-5bfa-add1-5c3fed61d13f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Outside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "d4bc50be-7125-55ef-9d29-c69af56e25d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12922" :question/problem "Evaluate $(1-4)^2 \\times \\dfrac{1}{12}$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1 - 4_(⏟)_(-3))^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{12} &= (-3)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-3)^{2}_(⏟)_(9) \\cdot \\frac{1}{12} &= 9 \\cdot \\frac{1}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9 \\cdot \\frac{1}{12} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{9}{1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{12} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{9 \\cdot 1}{1 \\cdot 12} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{9}{12} &=  \\\\\n\\frac{9 \\div 3}{12 \\div 3} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cc66e18-1adb-5bec-a6c6-f434ebf4ed13" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Inside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "21fccd11-6107-53b8-beb0-d0c39f23bc17" :question/math-academy-id "e-12923" :question/problem "What is the value of $\\left(5 \\div (-2)^2 \\right) \\times \\left(-\\dfrac{4}{5} \\right)$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, consider the expression inside the parenthesis:\n\n$$\n5 \\div (-2)^{2}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5 \\div (-2)^{2} &=  \\\\\n5 \\div 4 &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(5 \\div (-2)^{2}^(⏞)^(\\frac{5}{4})) \\cdot (-\\frac{4}{5}) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{5}{4} \\cdot (-\\frac{4}{5}) &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{5}{4} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{5 \\cdot 4}{4 \\cdot 5} &=  \\\\\n- \\frac{5 \\cdot 4}{4 \\cdot 5} &=  \\\\\n&= - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdadd355-0ce5-598a-b9cd-f189ccfb7ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a66648cb-8f77-50c9-893b-aedc4963bcc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052852} {:answer/id #uuid "b36b0693-1103-5abf-95a7-39b28db21c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052853} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa7a2bb-27be-5cfc-8be2-2abb2d0d90ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052854} {:answer/id #uuid "f546ef42-84c8-5376-84c5-ad082e37282c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052855} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7aa1a8-a1e0-58a3-9255-7868dd176226" :answer/type 